Q: How to get all &quot;rendered&quot; days from the Nuxt UI calendar component? A: <h1>Method 1 — Use <code>@update:visible-range</code> (Recommended)</h1>
<p><code>UCalendar</code> emits the visible date range when the month view changes.</p>
<h3>Example:</h3>
<pre><code>&lt;script setup&gt;
import { ref } from 'vue'

const visibleRange = ref(null)

function onRangeUpdate(range) {
  visibleRange.value = range
  console.log('Rendered range:', range)
}
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;template&gt;
  &lt;UCalendar
    @update:visible-range=&quot;onRangeUpdate&quot;
  /&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>The <code>range</code> object typically looks like:</p>
<pre><code>{
  start: Date,
  end: Date
}
</code></pre>
<p>Now you can generate <strong>all rendered days</strong> between <code>start</code> and <code>end</code>.</p>
<hr />
<h1>Method 2 — Use <code>v-model:page</code> (More Control)</h1>
<p>You can track the current displayed month.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;script setup&gt;
import { ref, computed } from 'vue'

const page = ref()

function getDaysInMonth(date) {
  const year = date.getFullYear()
  const month = date.getMonth()

  const first = new Date(year, month, 1)
  const last = new Date(year, month + 1, 0)

  const days = []
  let current = new Date(first)

  while (current &lt;= last) {
    days.push(new Date(current))
    current.setDate(current.getDate() + 1)
  }

  return days
}

const renderedDays = computed(() =&gt; {
  if (!page.value) return []
  return getDaysInMonth(page.value)
})
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;template&gt;
  &lt;UCalendar v-model:page=&quot;page&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;
</code></pre>
<hr />
<h1>If You Need EXACT Grid Days (Including Previous/Next Month Fillers)</h1>
<p>Calendar grids usually render:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Last few days of previous month</p>
</li>
<li><p>Current month days</p>
</li>
<li><p>First few days of next month</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>To get exactly what is displayed:</p>
<pre><code>function getRenderedGridDays(start, end) {
  const days = []
  let current = new Date(start)

  while (current &lt;= end) {
    days.push(new Date(current))
    current.setDate(current.getDate() + 1)
  }

  return days
}
</code></pre>

Q: Bash function to output variable&#39;s name and value A: <p>You can use <code>declare -n</code> to declare variables which are references to other variables</p>
<pre><code>foo() {
    declare -n boo=&quot;$1&quot;
    echo &quot;$1: $boo&quot;
}

goo=bar
foo goo # should print &quot;goo: bar&quot;
</code></pre>
